<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.gascity.pool-ceiling-engine</string>

  <!-- TEMPLATE — NOT INSTALLED (ga-m9x0lb.2). Installing it is slice 3 (Mayor, supervised), together with the one-line
       `include = [".gc/pool-ceiling-engine.toml"]` in city.toml, the first `touch .gc/pool-ceiling-engine.on` and the
       kill-switch drill. Order matters: create the EMPTY fragment BEFORE adding the include (an absent included fragment is
       a config load error), and only then bootstrap this job.

       The file is named *.plist.template ON PURPOSE, and the name is what keeps it uninstalled, not this comment. The deploy
       step (skill-integrity-install.sh scan_and_install_new_plists, run by the gascity rig's deploy_cmd on every merge)
       installs AND kickstarts every not-yet-loaded com.gascity.* file matching *.plist directly under this directory. Others
       read a *.plist name as "a job that must be loaded": daemon-refresh Step 1b (changed paths ending in .plist, verdict
       JOB_NOT_INSTALLED), the presence watchdog, the drift guard and the stale-daemon guard (the *.plist glob of this directory).
       pool-ceiling-wiring.selftest.sh section 1b runs the installer's own scan and fails if this label is selected. Slice 3
       puts it in service by copying it to ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.gascity.pool-ceiling-engine.plist by hand; renaming it
       to *.plist in this directory would make the NEXT deploy install and kickstart it, so do that only once
       pool-ceiling-engine.sh exists and honours the .on gate below.

       What it does every ~5 minutes: one sweep of pool-ceiling-engine.sh (see its header). It acts ONLY while
       $GC_CITY/.gc/pool-ceiling-engine.on exists; without it the run is silent and touches nothing. Kill switch:
       touch .gc/pool-ceiling-engine.off (the fragment is EMPTIED, never deleted).

       Why its own job, outside both dispatchers: the Pilot leaves its sweep early on quota / RAM / quiet hours, the gate only
       runs the ceiling step with a marker in the queue, and the Pilot sweeps every ~20 min. A ceiling that has to come DOWN
       under swap pressure cannot depend on either of them being awake.

       StartInterval 300 is far above the duration of one run (seconds), and the engine takes a single-instance lock with a
       TTL, so runs cannot pile up (ga-y0g5x: four overlapping guard instances once took bd down for the whole city).
       RunAtLoad is false, so a bootstrap or a relog does not start a sweep by itself. It does NOT stop a `launchctl kickstart`,
       and this repo's install_plist kickstarts after every bootstrap: the first run can happen at install time, and it is
       harmless only because of the .on gate above (the engine's contract, implemented and tested in slice B).

       GC_VARIABLE_SESSION_MAX is deliberately NOT set here: the engine reads the live value from the Pilot's plist
       (com.gascity.pilot.plist) so there is a single source of truth. If that plist is unreadable it falls back to 6, the
       dispatchers' own default — the direction that blocks raises. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq/packs/town-deltas/assets/pool-ceiling-engine.sh</string>
    <string>run</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq</string>

  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>300</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
  <key>LowPriorityIO</key><true/>
  <key>Nice</key><integer>10</integer>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq/.gc/logs/pool-ceiling-engine-launchd.out</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq/.gc/logs/pool-ceiling-engine-launchd.err</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/Users/athos/go/bin:/Users/athos/.local/bin</string>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>/Users/athos</string>
    <key>GC_CITY</key>
    <string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq</string>
    <key>GC_CITY_PATH</key>
    <string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq</string>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
